  "body": "From the independent review of PR #325 (#315, merged as be20197).\n\nThe new rotated-work-offset refusal (`crates/app/src/posting_wcs_rotation.rs`) measures the offset's total rotation angle and refuses anything above 1e-9 rad. A quaternion whose xyz parts are NaN or infinite falls through as \"unrotated\", so the offset would post as if it had no rotation. It is unchecked whether `SetWcsOrigin` (or the 3-2-1 align / project load paths) can ever store such a value; refusing it by name is the safe side either way.\n\nAlso noted: the setup sheet shows only the offset translation, so a rotation is invisible there.\n\n**Done means:** a non-finite offset rotation (or origin) is refused by name at command creation (`SetWcsOrigin`, align, project load) and in the post check; the setup sheet states the offset's rotation when it has one; pinned by tests.\n\nRelated: #315, PR #325, #196.\n",
